<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spanish Town</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as St. Jago de la Vega, Santiago de la Vega</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Spanish Town is a town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> founded by the Spanish around 1534 as Villa de la Vega, the capital of Spanish Jamaica. After the English conquest of 1655 it remained the island's capital and seat of its assembly until 1872, when the government moved to Kingston.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-town.jpg" alt="Spanish Town" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo by Not home (talk); Not home at en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St.-Jago-de-la-Vega.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
